text:
@ducatidave.b Yeah, I take your point. I'm living in SE Asia and all our roads are in very well maintained condition, so there are no problems with regard to ride comfort, suspension  or other problems people have complained about in Europe.
If I'm not mistaken the Jaecoo J7 had recently won in the UK  the car of the year 2026 award. Australia and NZ have also started the import and so far customers are happy with their purchase.
The J7 is being assembled in my own country (not China) and there are no problems with available spare parts and servicing. In case of a prolonged stay in the workshop I am being offered a car FOC in the meantime. Owned Porsche, BMW and VW before and I can live without lengthy stays in the workshop, because every damn part needs to be imported first, not to mention the exorbitant costs for maintenance.

@Joshifi3din the UK the base model is the Design with RWD and 309BHP, the Excellence has AWD and 523BHP. 
In ECO mode the Design is very relaxed in its feel, but in Sport it feels quicker than the quoted 5.9 secs 0-62mph time.
I feel that’s more than quick enough for day to day driving.

@BigLew-q4d1h  I never sold my soul to communists mate. USA Mega Corporations like Apple, Amazon, Tesla, General Motors, General Electric and General Dynamic all moved to China to build cheap factories to build their Products.
That wasn't me selling anyone out for Shareholder Profit mate. Morals haven't existed in the US Corporate Model since - When? Ever?
Australia might sell Iron Ore to China, but Corporate USA taught them how to manufacture stuff with it.
